From: Cencyte D <antiultra2007@gmail.com>
Subject: Add opt-in composition input sink objects for the x64 G HUB lab

Requires Wine10.20 patches0003,0004,0005,0011,0013. Regenerate requests
and syscall tables with tools/make_requests and tools/make_specfiles.
Build and mount Win32u, ntdll and wineserver as a matched set.

Observed InputStateManager descriptor: four type2 routes to the same
message-only HWND. Local Windows win32kbase reference establishes the
Composition object type, LUID/view storage and ordinary NtClose lifetime.
Only x64 zero-metadata routes0/1/2 and descriptor sizes0xe8/0x128 are
accepted. Cross-process HWND creation is deliberately rejected in this
prototype. WINE_GHUB_INPUT_SINK=1 enables creation. This provides the
object/binding foundation, not composition hit testing or input dispatch.

